      "name": "Experimental Pipelines Ontology (XPO)",
      "abstract": "Experimental Pipelines Ontology (XPO) is a high-level ontology for modelling experimental pipelines and procedures across scientific domains. The core modelling primitives are 'sample' (a continuant) and 'operation' (an occurrent) such that operations are applied to samples and produce other samples; the ontology defines annotation and object properties (e.g. hasApparatus, depicts, hasAffiliation) to describe relationships and metadata about samples, operations, apparatus, people, and institutions. The source is an OWL file hosted in the PlantExpAssay Bitbucket repository and imports BFO; it is intended to provide reusable terms and relations for describing experimental workflows and related metadata.",
